	(text
		"ALEC SENSOR S0 — electrical study; no PCB or ingress qualification.\n3 AA primary cells; no charging. USB-C is data-only: batteries + SW1 ON required.\nSW1 is a hard battery disconnect; DC current rating, fuse and package are OPEN design items.\nRTC time survives ESP deep sleep, but is lost on SW1 OFF or battery removal. Resync before arming."
		(at 22.86 23 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27))
			(justify left bottom))
		(uuid 17073ee8-ba24-5499-b73b-0f7609b0b531))
	(text
		"3.31 V always on with SW1 closed. 4.985 V radar rail: GPIO16 high = ON.\nR19 holds radar OFF during reset; PS/SYNC high permits power-save operation.\nReserve >=200 mA at the radar connector; measure startup at depleted-cell voltage."
		(at 22.86 248 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27))
			(justify left bottom))
		(uuid 9dea0a8d-b0cb-514a-a18b-bb909a60967e))
	(text
		"GPIO17 TX -> radar RX; GPIO18 RX <- radar TX. UART: 256000 8N1.\nGPIO4 = presence wake. GPIO11 = I/O switch enable, default OFF.\nPower up: I/O OFF -> rail ON -> PG valid -> I/O ON -> fresh valid frames.\nPower down: I/O OFF -> UART stop -> rail OFF. OUT cannot wake if radar is off."
		(at 22.86 271 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27))
			(justify left bottom))
		(uuid c03c8252-368a-5a60-accf-43757189cf1f))
	(text
		"RV-3028: I2C GPIO8 SDA / GPIO9 SCL; interrupt GPIO1 (active LOW).\nShort press GPIO10: battery; long press: physical pairing.\nRGB common anode; GPIO38/39/40 LOW lights R/G/B.\nNo always-on power LED. Use low-duty PWM for presence indication."
		(at 270 205 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27))
			(justify left bottom))
		(uuid 1f772032-8a85-519c-adc1-683705eb9ae6))
	(text
		"Schematic study only. Switch, protection, connector retention,\nradome and wet-room behavior must be resolved before PCB release."
		(at 270 248 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27))
			(justify left bottom))
		(uuid e5f81bd1-9d26-5be7-8619-7daa5562beb9)))
